 that's  that's usually happening its  rockets on cities  you're not too far from the embattled  nuclear power plant at zafaria is  shelling and fighting still going on  there  yeah that's what we're hearing shelling  has been happening constantly throughout  the past few weeks i must say um and  it seems according to the russian  occupational authorities that this night  again some shells have landed in the  town nearby where the  the the  power plants um  engineers etc live  and  not on the site of the plant itself but  in the past few days we've also seen  something hitting there so um  yes uh this uh  this area is is embattled and uh the  dangers are still there an international  inspector is set to arrive at the plan  tomorrow will they get full and safe  access to the site  nobody knows that i mean there is an  agreement basically that they can travel  there russia has said it will give them  access but what will be on site nobody  knows  what precautions are being taken against  a potential radiation leak  there are many uh security systems in a  nuclear power plant the  reactors themselves are pretty sturdy  as far as we've been hearing a shell  wouldn't be able to break that and and  open up the reactor and release the  energy but the weakest spot are the  cooling systems even if the reactors are  shut off  they need to be cooled for several  months until  the the fuel has really cooled down  enough so it's  safe to leave it without cooling and  these systems they're dependent on  electricity and the most uh dangerous  thing is plus possibly an electricity  cut we've been pretty close to that a  few days ago when the when the plant was  taken off the grid there are generators  that are then supplying uh the energy  but that seems to be the most critical  point to what extent russia has taken  precautions on site enough fuel etc we  don't know that's something the iaea  will have to figure out when they're on  site  mathias berger in zaparicio for us thank  